<title>JAPAN: Japan Jan corn imports rise 13.6 pct yr/yr - MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan Jan corn imports rise 13.6 pct yr/yr - MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's corn imports in January totalled 1,333,733 tonnes, up 13.6 percent from a year earlier, Finance Ministry data showed on Friday.</p>
<p>Details were as follows, in tonnes:</p>
<p>			  Jan 97	  Dec 96	  Jan 96</p>
<p> Total		1,333,733     1,434,204     1,174,557</p>
<p> Feed corn total    870,016     1,034,537	 755,426</p>
<p> Others		 463,717	 399,667	 419,131</p>
<p>Top suppliers of feed corn (in tonnes):</p>
<p> U.S.		   859,934     1,015,844	 755,426</p>
<p> Argentina		  nil	   5,000	     nil</p>
<p> South Africa	  10,082	  11,808	     nil</p>
<p>Total feed corn imports throughout calendar 1996 reached 11,453,034 tonnes against 11,681,998 tonnes a year earlier.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodity Desk (+81-3 3432-7391)</p>
</text>
